ios: world map

For the mobile HUD's World map window. The 2004 map applet (MapView, upstream's port of Jagex's website map) runs in
an iframe of its own (web/host/mapview.html) as MobileMapView, a subclass with a phone's controls in place of the
applet's buttons and keys: drag to pan (it glides on), pinch to zoom, double-tap to zoom in, a two-finger tap to zoom
out. Zooming settles on the applet's four zooms, the only ones its labels are drawn at. It marks the player, draws the
applet's overview on request, flashes a key's icons (gliding to the nearest when none is in view) and shows the map
the player is on (the surface, the underground or the other places: MapView's three maps). The host drives it with
postMessage (see MobileMapView.ts).

MapView's grids are columns of typed arrays: as nested plain arrays its 1600x1408 tiles took ~96 MB of JS heap.

hudPlayerTile() gives the world tile the local player stands on.

